invariant: INV-14
file: quic_token.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the window refuses only a token that is too old, so a token whose
  issue instant is after now_seconds checks. A process whose clock runs
  ahead of another that holds the same key then mints tokens the other
  accepts for as long as the gap between the two clocks, whatever the
  lifetime. The window case requires a token issued one second after now to
  be refused.

--- old
    if (now_seconds < issued_seconds || now_seconds - issued_seconds > lifetime_seconds) {
--- new
    if (now_seconds > issued_seconds && now_seconds - issued_seconds > lifetime_seconds) {
